cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite it as below, and cite the CropGlobe
  benchmark it is built on (Tong & Wang, arXiv:2509.03497).
title: "Zero-overlap PPI: prediction-powered inference when the labelling probability is zero"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible study on CropGlobe of what labels from other countries can
  say about a country with none: a positivity diagnostic, transported
  prediction-powered corrections, partial-identification bounds computed by
  linear programming, and design-based inference from a small sample inside
  the target.
authors:
  - family-names: Bali
    given-names: Rohan
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-22
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rohanbalixz/zero-overlap-ppi"
keywords:
  - prediction-powered inference
  - partial identification
  - distribution shift
  - remote sensing
  - crop mapping
